{:edb/db-before-t 502 :edb/db-after-t 503 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533815 50 #inst "2026-10-05T03:13:12.441Z" 13194139533815 true] [17592186068808 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253139 13194139533815 true] [17592186068808 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253146 13194139533815 true] [17592186068808 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253153 13194139533815 true] [17592186068808 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253211 13194139533815 true] [17592186068808 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253218 13194139533815 true] [17592186068809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253160 13194139533815 true] [17592186068809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253181 13194139533815 true] [17592186068809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253188 13194139533815 true] [17592186068809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253191 13194139533815 true] [17592186068809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253225 13194139533815 true] [17592186068810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253194 13194139533815 true] [17592186068810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253198 13194139533815 true] [17592186068810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253201 13194139533815 true] [17592186068810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253232 13194139533815 true] [17592186068811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253167 13194139533815 true] [17592186068811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253174 13194139533815 true] [17592186068811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253204 13194139533815 true] [17592186068811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186253207 13194139533815 true] [17592186069202 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533815 true] [17592186069202 1145 "We note that $b=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nThe equation has the denominators $36b$ and $12{b}^{2}.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(36b,12{b}^{2})=36{b}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $36{b}^{2},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}} & =-\\frac{12}{36b}+\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}} \\\\ 36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =36{b}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b}+\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =36{b}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b})+36{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 3\\cdot 12{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) & =b\\cdot 36b\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{36b})+3\\cdot 12{b}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{12{b}^{2}}) \\\\ 3\\cdot \\cancel{12{b}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{5b+8}{\\cancel{12{b}^{2}}}) & =b\\cdot \\cancel{36b}\\cdot (-\\frac{12}{\\cancel{36b}})+3\\cdot \\cancel{12{b}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{4b+8}{\\cancel{12{b}^{2}}}) \\\\ 3(5b+8) & =-12b+3(4b+8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $b,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(5b+8) & =-12b+3(4b+8) \\\\ 15b+24 & =-12b+12b+24 \\\\ 15b+24 & =24 \\\\ 15b & =24-24 \\\\ 15b & =0 \\\\ b & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $b=0$ as a solution. Since $b=0,$ we conclude that there is no solution." 13194139533815 true] [17592186069442 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533815 true] [17592186069442 1145 "We note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $x,2x,$ and $4x.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(x,2x,4x)=4x.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4x,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{2+x}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x} \\\\ 4x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) & =4x\\cdot (\\frac{2+x}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x}) \\\\ 4x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) & =4x\\cdot (\\frac{2+x}{2x})+4x\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4x}) \\\\ 4x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) & =2\\cdot 2x\\cdot (\\frac{2+x}{2x})+4x\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4x}) \\\\ 4\\cancel{x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\cancel{x}}) & =2\\cdot \\cancel{2x}\\cdot (\\frac{2+x}{\\cancel{2x}})+\\cancel{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{\\cancel{4x}}) \\\\ 4\\cdot (1) & =2\\cdot (2+x)+3 \\\\ 4 & =2(2+x)+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $x,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2(2+x)+3 \\\\ 4 & =4+2x+3 \\\\ 2x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $x=0$ as a solution. But since $x=-\\frac{3}{2}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253140 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1089 "q-115788" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1100 "Solve for $m$ where $\\frac{3m-1}{{m}^{3}}+\\frac{m+2}{{m}^{3}}=\\frac{2m+3}{{m}^{3}}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1113 #uuid "ffcdf275-e056-5057-8270-11fc9a6292de" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253139 1145 "First, we note that $m=0$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by ${m}^{3},$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3m-1}{{m}^{3}}+\\frac{m+2}{{m}^{3}} & =\\frac{2m+3}{{m}^{3}} \\\\ {m}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{3m-1}{{m}^{3}}+\\frac{m+2}{{m}^{3}}) & ={m}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2m+3}{{m}^{3}}) \\\\ {m}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3m-1}{{m}^{3}}+{m}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{m+2}{{m}^{3}} & ={m}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{2m+3}{{m}^{3}} \\\\ \\cancel{{m}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{3m-1}{\\cancel{{m}^{3}}}+\\cancel{{m}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{m+2}{\\cancel{{m}^{3}}} & =\\cancel{{m}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{2m+3}{\\cancel{{m}^{3}}} \\\\ 3m-1+m+2 & =2m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $m,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3m-1+m+2 & =2m+3 \\\\ 4m+1 & =2m+3 \\\\ 4m-2m & =3-1 \\\\ 2m & =2 \\\\ m & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $m=0$ as a solution. But since $m=1\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $m=1.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253141 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253142 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253143 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253144 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253145 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1041 "selection" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253142 13194139533815 true] [17592186253140 1110 #uuid "0a317f28-d321-56f8-8d64-6f2a99feb03e" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253141 1034 "2" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253141 1111 #uuid "24a4aeee-88ab-5aff-8e3e-50694ddbc401" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253142 1034 "1" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253142 1111 #uuid "45934fab-b7ef-54c6-892c-926d34e2d828" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253143 1034 "-3" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253143 1111 #uuid "991aec93-e276-545d-8913-e0550aceb660" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253144 1034 "4" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253144 1111 #uuid "807e495c-435d-51b8-9f54-bae8720e3280" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253145 1034 "-1" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253145 1111 #uuid "37035c74-5b01-5f88-be92-14119e86d022" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253147 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1089 "q-115791" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1100 "Solve for $z$ where $\\frac{z+1}{2z}=2-\\frac{2z+1}{2z}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1113 #uuid "c7e93f25-c681-5303-8b0f-eaffed982cfc" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253146 1145 "First, we note that $z=0$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by $2z,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z+1}{2z} & =2-\\frac{2z+1}{2z} \\\\ 2z\\cdot (\\frac{z+1}{2z}) & =2z\\cdot (2-\\frac{2z+1}{2z}) \\\\ 2z\\cdot \\frac{z+1}{2z} & =2z\\cdot 2-2z\\cdot \\frac{2z+1}{2z} \\\\ \\cancel{2z}\\cdot \\frac{z+1}{\\cancel{2z}} & =2z\\cdot 2-\\cancel{2z}\\cdot \\frac{2z+1}{\\cancel{2z}} \\\\ z+1 & =4z-(2z+1) \\\\ z+1 & =4z-2z-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $z,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =4z-2z-1 \\\\ z+1 & =2z-1 \\\\ -z & =-2 \\\\ z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $z=0$ as a solution. But since $z=2\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $z=2.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253148 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253149 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253150 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253151 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253152 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1041 "selection" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253151 13194139533815 true] [17592186253147 1110 #uuid "64cddbcd-5541-5889-a231-e5fecc8e2564" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253148 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253148 1111 #uuid "4c9e733e-fe10-582c-9f6a-6867ab241d20" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253149 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253149 1111 #uuid "701ef8e2-c225-5250-9bbf-3424b2f290db" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253150 1034 "No solution" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533815 true] [17592186253150 1111 #uuid "95d562e6-c1ad-52c0-806f-0d6089d60b30" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253151 1034 "2" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253151 1111 #uuid "778881e4-b5f1-546a-90b6-30cbad641ce0" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253152 1034 "-2" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253152 1111 #uuid "9bf1a9e4-97fd-50c0-9b8c-4cc59a485297" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253154 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1089 "q-115792" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1100 "Solve for $w$ where $1-\\frac{2w-3}{3w}=\\frac{w+5}{3w}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1113 #uuid "d2ad4702-d44d-5f4e-8f5e-d045030201d4" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253153 1145 "First, we note that $w=0$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nWe multiply both sides of the equation by $3w,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{2w-3}{3w} & =\\frac{w+5}{3w} \\\\ 3w\\cdot (1-\\frac{2w-3}{3w}) & =3w\\cdot (\\frac{w+5}{3w}) \\\\ 3w\\cdot 1-3w\\cdot \\frac{2w-3}{3w} & =3w\\cdot \\frac{w+5}{3w} \\\\ 3w-\\cancel{3w}\\cdot \\frac{2w-3}{\\cancel{3w}} & =\\cancel{3w}\\cdot \\frac{w+5}{\\cancel{3w}} \\\\ 3w-(2w-3) & =w+5 \\\\ 3w-2w+3 & =w+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $w,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w-2w+3 & =w+5 \\\\ w+3 & =w+5 \\\\ w-w & =5-3 \\\\ 0 & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a false statement. Therefore, we conclude that there is no solution." 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253155 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253156 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253157 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253158 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253159 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1041 "selection" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253156 13194139533815 true] [17592186253154 1110 #uuid "e9a84872-9084-5fa2-b3c6-ab9cb044a488" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253155 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253155 1111 #uuid "f911ff0f-7835-5ee8-898a-f06fbe0aac29" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253156 1034 "No solution" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533815 true] [17592186253156 1111 #uuid "ee4515cc-4711-5465-ad6c-18f44ce16b6c" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253157 1034 "2" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253157 1111 #uuid "d237e7e0-647e-55ee-9123-6191b1fd36d6" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253158 1034 "1" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253158 1111 #uuid "01e28e57-5180-526d-9ad4-f6d14efbe207" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253159 1034 "-1" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253159 1111 #uuid "687a021a-5d51-56af-98e8-b3ae149c4b7a" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253161 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1089 "q-115794" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1100 "Which value of $z$ satisfies the equation $\\frac{2z-1}{6z}=\\frac{3z-1}{3z}+\\frac{z-1}{6z}?$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1113 #uuid "2691c2ad-adb0-5c66-a320-3594e74b4de1" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253160 1145 "We note that $z=0$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nThe equation has the denominators $3z$ and $6z.$ So first, we find the least common multiple (or $\\text{LCM}$) of the denominators. We find that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(3z,6z)=6z.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $6z,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2z-1}{6z}=\\frac{3z-1}{3z}+\\frac{z-1}{6z} \\\\ 6z\\cdot (\\frac{2z-1}{6z}) & =6z\\cdot (\\frac{3z-1}{3z}+\\frac{z-1}{6z}) \\\\ 6z\\cdot (\\frac{2z-1}{6z}) & =6z\\cdot (\\frac{3z-1}{3z})+6z\\cdot (\\frac{z-1}{6z}) \\\\ \\cancel{6z}\\cdot (\\frac{2z-1}{\\cancel{6z}}) & =2\\cdot \\cancel{3z}\\cdot (\\frac{3z-1}{\\cancel{3z}})+\\cancel{6z}\\cdot (\\frac{z-1}{\\cancel{6z}}) \\\\ 2z-1 & =2\\cdot (3z-1)+z-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $z,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-1 & =2(3z-1)+z-1 \\\\ 2z-1 & =6z-2+z-1 \\\\ 2z-1 & =7z-3 \\\\ 2z-7z & =-3+1 \\\\ -5z & =-2 \\\\ z & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $z=0$ as a solution. But since $z=\\frac{2}{5}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $z=\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253162 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253163 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253164 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253165 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253166 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1041 "selection" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253164 13194139533815 true] [17592186253161 1110 #uuid "50006c08-45ae-52df-a09e-7c19aa9370fb" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253162 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253162 1111 #uuid "32dc52ed-b5e1-59d7-9ea7-2652d96a2234" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253163 1034 "No solution" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533815 true] [17592186253163 1111 #uuid "89c014a0-0c9b-5552-a18d-044d0784a040" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253164 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253164 1111 #uuid "5b320f40-9600-53a1-97f1-49c94f0cfcd3" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253