 that\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(3m,5m,15m)=15m.\n$$\n\nSo, we multiply both sides of the equation by $15m,$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2m-3}{3m}+\\frac{m+5}{5m} & =\\frac{m+4}{15m} \\\\ 15m\\cdot (\\frac{2m-3}{3m}+\\frac{m+5}{5m}) & =15m\\cdot (\\frac{m+4}{15m}) \\\\ 15m\\cdot (\\frac{2m-3}{3m})+15m\\cdot (\\frac{m+5}{5m}) & =15m\\cdot (\\frac{m+4}{15m}) \\\\ 5\\cdot 3m\\cdot (\\frac{2m-3}{3m})+3\\cdot 5m\\cdot (\\frac{m+5}{5m}) & =15m\\cdot (\\frac{m+4}{15m}) \\\\ 5\\cdot \\cancel{3m}\\cdot (\\frac{2m-3}{\\cancel{3m}})+3\\cdot \\cancel{5m}\\cdot (\\frac{m+5}{\\cancel{5m}}) & =\\cancel{15m}\\cdot (\\frac{m+4}{\\cancel{15m}}) \\\\ 5(2m-3)+3(m+5) & =m+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have a linear equation in $m,$ and we can solve this using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(2m-3)+3(m+5) & =m+4 \\\\ 10m-15+3m+15 & =m+4 \\\\ 13m & =m+4 \\\\ 12m & =4 \\\\ m & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall that we cannot allow $m=0$ as a solution. But since $m=\\frac{1}{3}\\ne 0,$ we conclude that the solution is $m=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253234 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253235 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253236 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253237 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253238 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1041 "selection" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253237 13194139533815 true] [17592186253233 1110 #uuid "f999c9f2-c51c-5624-92bc-e401a0332ea7" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253234 1034 "-\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533815 true] [17592186253234 1111 #uuid "6e87fa72-a14e-5be9-93d6-4dded0403756" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253235 1034 "2" 13194139533815 true] [17592186253235 1103 #edb/